{title: God Moves in a Mysterious Way}
{artist: William Cowper / Scottish Psalter (1615)}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: D}
{key_original: Eb}
{tempo: 105}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The Methodist Hymnal (New York: Methodist Publishing House, 1939), # 68)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]God moves in [A]a myste[D]rious [G]way
[D]His [A]won[Bm]ders [G]to [A]per[D]form;
[D]He plants [A]His [Bm]footsteps in [E]the [A]sea
[D]And [Em]rides upon [A]the [D]storm.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Deep in un[A]fathomable [D]mines
[G]Of [D]nev[A]er [Bm]fail[G]ing [A]skill
[D]He treasures [A]up [Bm]His bright de[E]signs
[A]And [D]works [Em]His sover[A]eign [D]will.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Ye fearful [A]saints, fresh cour[D]age [G]take;
[D]The [A]clouds [Bm]ye [G]so [A]much [D]dread
[D]Are big [A]with [Bm]mercy and [E]shall [A]break
[D]In [Em]blessings on [A]your [D]head.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]Judge not the [A]Lord by fee[D]ble [G]sense,
[D]But [A]trust [Bm]Him [G]for [A]His [D]grace;
[D]Behind [A]a [Bm]frowning pro[E]vi[A]dence
[D]He [Em]hides a smil[A]ing [D]face.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
[D]Blind unbe[A]lief is sure [D]to [G]err
[D]And [A]scan [Bm]His [G]work [A]in [D]vain;
[D]God is [A]His [Bm]own inter[E]pret[A]er,
[D]And [Em]He will make [A]it [D]plain.
{end_of_verse}
